<header class="ed-hero bg-inverse pb-14 pt-32 text-inverse-ink md:pt-40"><div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6"><p class="mb-4 text-sm font-bold uppercase tracking-widest text-accent">The Naked Tech field guide</p><h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight md:text-5xl">Set up a new home printer without guesswork</h1><p class="ed-deck">Start with the exact model, choose a suitable connection, then check printing and scanning separately.</p></div></header>
<article class="ed-guide bg-canvas py-12 md:py-16" aria-label="Set up a new home printer without guesswork"><div class="ed-layout">
{{ contents([{"id": "start", "title": "Find your starting point"}, {"id": "identify-the-equipment", "title": "Identify the equipment"}, {"id": "choose-a-connection", "title": "Choose a connection"}, {"id": "add-the-printer", "title": "Add the printer to your device"}, {"id": "check-each-function", "title": "Check each function"}, {"id": "related", "title": "What to read next"}]) }}
<div class="ed-reading guide-reading text-lg">
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A new printer is easier to set up when you treat it as three separate jobs: prepare the equipment, connect it to one device, and check the functions you intend to use. The exact model and operating system matter. Keep the manufacturer instructions nearby, use supported software, and avoid assuming that every printer, phone or network behaves the same way.</p>
<section class="ed-start" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-heading"><p class="ed-label">Start here</p><h2 id="start-heading">Start with the exact model</h2><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Before opening settings, record the printer’s full model name and check the instructions for your operating system.</p><div class="ed-choices">
{{ choice("Identify the equipment", "Find the exact model, supported operating systems and the manufacturer’s setup instructions before choosing software or cables.", "#identify-the-equipment", "startup", "/img/guides/printer-field-guide-v1.webp", "A household printer with a sheet of paper.", "Read this part") }}
{{ choice("Choose one connection", "Use either a suitable existing Wi-Fi network or a compatible USB connection, following the model’s instructions.", "#choose-a-connection", "applications", "/img/guides/printer-field-guide-v1.webp", "A laptop and connection cable.", "Read this part") }}
{{ choice("Check each function", "Test ordinary printing and scanning separately. A successful print does not prove that scanning is ready.", "#check-each-function", "online", "/img/guides/printer-field-guide-v1.webp", "A magnifying glass over a printed test page.", "Read this part") }}
</div></section>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="identify-the-equipment"><span aria-hidden="true">01</span>Identify the equipment</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Write down the exact printer model, rather than just the brand. Check whether the model supports the computer or mobile device you plan to use and read the manufacturer’s instructions for that combination.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For Windows 11, open <strong>Settings &gt; Bluetooth &amp; devices &gt; Printers &amp; scanners</strong> and check whether the printer is already listed before selecting <em>Add device</em>. Use current software from Windows Update or the manufacturer’s official support page. Avoid unofficial driver sites and do not install a package merely because its name looks similar.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For an iPhone or iPad, wireless printing depends on an AirPrint-enabled printer and a compatible setup. Not every app supports printing. See <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/109349">Apple’s AirPrint instructions</a> for the supported process.</p>{% call note("info", "Before you buy", "Compare the whole running cost") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Record the pages you expect to print in a typical month, whether they are mostly black-and-white or colour, whether duplex printing or scanning matters, and which paper sizes you need. For each researched candidate, check the exact manufacturer-specified cartridge or toner yield, current consumable price, paper requirements, optional subscription or automatic-replenishment terms, and support for your devices. A simple consumable estimate is price divided by stated yield, but yields use test conditions and are not a promise of your actual cost. This is a comparison worksheet, not a brand ranking or endorsement.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="choose-a-connection"><span aria-hidden="true">02</span>Choose a connection</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Choose the connection described for your model. A wireless setup normally requires the printer and device to use the same household network. Do not assume that a particular Wi-Fi band, extender or guest network will work unless the manufacturer says it will.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A direct USB connection can be simpler where the printer and primary device are close together. Use a compatible cable and follow the manual’s order of steps. If the instructions ask you to install software before connecting the cable, follow that sequence rather than improvising.</p>{% call note("care", "Take care", "protect your accounts") %}<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Review account, privacy and subscription choices as they appear. Enter passwords and verification codes yourself. Do not share them with anyone helping remotely or in person.</p>{% endcall %}
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="add-the-printer"><span aria-hidden="true">03</span>Add the printer to your device</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Install only the software needed for the exact model and intended device. During setup, check the selected printer name and connection before accepting. If Windows already shows the printer, use that existing entry rather than repeatedly adding duplicates.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">On a phone or tablet, use the manufacturer’s supported app or the operating system’s supported print action where appropriate. If an app cannot print, that may be a limitation of the app rather than proof that the printer is faulty.</p>
<h2 class="ed-section-heading" id="check-each-function"><span aria-hidden="true">04</span>Check each function</h2>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Print one ordinary, harmless page first. Confirm that the text is legible, the paper size is correct and the page is not unexpectedly cropped. If the printer is multifunction, test scanning separately with the manufacturer’s supported software and save the result to an intended folder.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">Record what worked and what you have not tested. A completed connection is not the same as proof that every feature, account option or future device will work. For Windows scanning details, use <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/hardware/printer/install-and-use-a-scanner-in-windows">Microsoft’s scanner guidance</a>. For Windows printer installation details, see <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/hardware/printer/add-or-install-a-printer-in-windows">Microsoft’s printer guidance</a>.</p><p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">If an existing printer has stopped working, use the <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="/guides/printer-not-printing-first-checks/">printer troubleshooting checks</a> instead.</p>
<p class="mb-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">For setup steps, use the instructions for your exact printer and consumables. If relevant, see <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.apple.com/en-au/109349">Apple’s AirPrint instructions</a> or <a class="font-semibold text-accent-ink underline underline-offset-4 hover:text-ink" href="https://support.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/hardware/printer/add-or-install-a-printer-in-windows">Microsoft’s printer installation guidance</a>.</p>
